\"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9e9aaf9cf0745b451b01a2e530078f7b21147cd1e4cdceefebc13ea72f29e7ed","event_uuid":"cb4383bd-fffe-46d1-ace4-8eb1148fb2c1","position":{"commit_sha":"bfaa075d34f61461b9e9d5a0dc374a50b72f6926","position":"1786651370239902001-cb4383bd-fffe-46d1-ace4-8eb1148fb2c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c7e10066710f6aa18fc6e7e15a8984c774146a32ccfff08a6fe3a7cc3b25f6ac","event_uuid":"dc277d67-2d71-4a96-8bf1-7678e18ad188","position":{"commit_sha":"bfaa075d34f61461b9e9d5a0dc374a50b72f6926","position":"1786651371829932001-dc277d67-2d71-4a96-8bf1-7678e18ad188"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"71196381083c0717d87e43fa52705784c6ec37268ef91ef7c5a6cdb7f561562a","event_uuid":"08bda40e-3c10-4465-9bdb-2efedc72f859","position":{"commit_sha":"c0557bcf5e3ffb40372c7b1de3af3e62313765f5","position":"1786652110038386422-08bda40e-3c10-4465-9bdb-2efedc72f859"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786162200231243001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"08bda40e-3c10-4465-9bdb-2efedc72f859","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4294-d295-80ab-4995"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` measures **777 lines** against the hard 800-line module-size gate\n(`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), which CI enforces with no allowlist. The sibling story that\nprojects two new ticket state fields needs more than the 23 remaining lines.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract the STATUS-processing cluster into a new `_processors_status.py`: `_fold_plan_review_phase`\n(`:32-38`), `_fold_claimed_session` (`:187-208`), `_fold_close_class` (`:211-225`) and\n`process_status` (`:228-328`).\n\nThe seam already exists and is closed: `process_status` is the **sole caller** of all three folds,\nat `:279,281,282` in the fork-winner branch and `:307,308,309` in the normal branch. The one function\nthat might have made the cluster leaky does not — `process_snapshot` sets `plan_review_phase` inline\nat `:705-710` rather than calling `_fold_plan_review_phase`.\n\nThe sibling `_processors_identity.py` (179 lines) is the exact precedent, and its own header states\nthe contract this follows: it imports nothing from `_processors`, so the split stays one-way, and\n`_processors` re-exports every symbol for back-compat. The re-export block at `_processors.py:15-22`\nis the pattern to mirror.\n\nThe alternative cut — the CREATE/genesis cluster (`process_create` `:40-152` plus\n`_project_legacy_creation_channel` `:155-184`, 143 lines) — is also valid but strictly weaker:\n`_project_legacy_creation_channel` has a second caller in `process_snapshot` (`:777`), so the\nextracted symbol would have to be imported back. The STATUS cluster has no such back-edge.\n\nThis is a behaviour-preserving move: no logic is rewritten.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py` (new) — the moved cluster, ~171 lines\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` — drops to ~632 lines, plus a re-export line\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new behaviour, so the oracle is the existing suite passing unchanged. This extraction is the\ncheapest of the set — the new module's only import is `logging`, and it touches no other module-level\nname — so the risk concentrates entirely on the re-export:\n\n- Re-export assertion: `from rebar.reducer._processors import process_status` still resolves. The\n  complete consumer set is **seven** importers, all of which must stay green with **zero** edits:\n  two in production — `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py` (multi-line import at `:19,32`, used in the\n  dispatch table at `:97`) and `src/rebar/reducer/__init__.py` (`:39`, re-exported in `__all__` at\n  `:76`) — and five test modules: `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13,17`,\n  `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10`, `tests/unit/test_harness_provenance.py:20`,\n  `tests/unit/test_claimed_session.py:20`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_happy.py:6`.\n  Two of these use multi-line `from ._processors import (...)` blocks and are invisible to a\n  single-line grep for `import process_status`, so the inventory must be derived with a\n  multi-line-aware search rather than a one-line pattern.\n- Replay equivalence: replaying a fixture ticket through the reducer yields byte-identical state\n  before and after the move. This is the assertion that actually proves behaviour preservation for a\n  reducer, since a status fold silently dropping would still leave a passing import.\n- One-way import: `_processors_status` must not import `_processors`, asserted directly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_processors.py` and `_processors_status.py` are each at or below 650 lines; checked by the\n      module-size gate with both counts recorded.\n- [ ] `process_status` still resolves from `rebar.reducer._processors` and from `rebar.reducer`;\n      checked by importing it by both paths and running all five named test modules unedited.\n- [ ] Replaying a fixture ticket yields byte-identical compiled state before and after; checked by\n      comparing the serialized state against a pre-move capture.\n- [ ] `_processors_status.py` imports nothing from `_processors`; checked by an explicit assertion on\n      the module's imports.\n- [ ] The full existing test suite passes with no test-file edits; checked by the gating test command.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py","reason":"new module receiving the STATUS cluster and its three folds"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","reason":"drops to ~632 lines and re-exports the moved symbols"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py","reason":"re-export resolution and byte-identical replay equivalence"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","4294-d295-80ab-4995"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"cb4383bd-fffe-46d1-ace4-8eb1148fb2c1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ce02-47ed-6505-4925","ticket_type":"story","title":"Size relief: extract the STATUS cluster from reducer/_processors.py into _processors_status.py","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b2be2bc3-9cab-4d93-b9f1-6162b67bc451","b2ae9d60-6c4e-4634-a158-da666c406d23","e6474b3d-b0c2-49a5-b752-bebe1723d041","c7f40058-6e4a-4c13-9cd7-27b04ccff8ce","f00635ad-5acf-465c-9621-f15c23cdfe9f","38dbb0d4-e03d-466a-a220-a89a5afbeda1","7fd2b0c7-5644-4d20-a625-cd64530e0a34","cb4383bd-fffe-46d1-ace4-8eb1148fb2c1","dc277d67-2d71-4a96-8bf1-7678e18ad188","08bda40e-3c10-4465-9bdb-2efedc72f859"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786652110038386423,"uuid":"f2722b4a-4240-4882-bb05-35388206b0c5"}